<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Straubing</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Straubing is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-bavaria">Lower Bavaria</a>, at the centre of the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauboden">Gäuboden</a> plain. From 1353 to 1425 it was the capital of the Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing, whose dukes also ruled Hainaut and Holland and built its ducal castle, and in 1435 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agnes-bernauer">Agnes Bernauer</a> was drowned there. Its old town is dominated by a 14th-century city tower.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/straubing.jpg" alt="Straubing" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benutzer:Donaulustig · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Straubinger_Stadtbild.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
